{
  "name": "Free timestamp",
  "description": "Two camera layers on one face. The first places its fetched-at chip freely (`timestampX`/`timestampY` name the chip's centre as fractions of the layer's own box); the second keeps a corner and must carry no coordinates at all. Both resolvers have to pass the pair through untouched, and the second element pins the fallback: a document that never left the corners still resolves with `timestampCorner` in charge and the pair absent. The free element also writes a derived `timestampCorner` on the wire, set to whichever corner the point is nearest, so a watch that predates the pair lands the chip near the mark.",
